{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.instH3WedderburnReassembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.instH3WedderburnReassembly","kind":"instance","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L154-L163","doc":"The numerical witness pin: the H_3 Wedderburn reassembly residual\nat `q_0` is 2.22e-16, below the 1 ppQ floor. The literal value is\npulled from `option-e-phase1-h3-cross-check.witness.json` (Python\ncross-check), with the floating-point bound encoded here so Lean\ndownstream consumers see the precision tag. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.residual_below_ppq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.residual_below_ppq","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The recorded residual is at or below the 1 ppQ precision floor\n(10⁻¹⁵), satisfying L1 compute precision per AGENTS.md. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.max_residual_eps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.max_residual_eps","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L149-L149","doc":"Max single-entry residual of the Wedderburn-sum reassembly\nvs the published H_3 NF-basis Gram, in float64 epsilon units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.H3WedderburnReassembly","kind":"class","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L129-L152","doc":"**Witness-recorded Wedderburn-sum identity at H_3.** Records the\nstructural identity verified by the Python cross-check\n\n  `tr_M(b_i · b_j) = Σ_{λ ⊢ 3} y_λ · tr(ρ_λ(b_i) · ρ_λ(b_j))`\n\nfor the H_3 NF basis `{1, σ_1, σ_2, σ_1σ_2, σ_2σ_1, σ_1σ_2σ_1}`\n(21 unique entries). The canonical instance is the Python\nwitness `option-e-phase1-h3-cross-check.witness.json`:\n\n* `max_residual := 2.22e-16` (float64 epsilon, well below\n  the 1 ppQ ≡ 10⁻¹⁵ acceptance bar from AGENTS.md §Precision goals);\n* `rms_residual := 1.14e-16` (RMS across 36 NF Gram entries).\n\nFollowing the `BraidWordBasisGram.lean` pattern in this directory,\nthe class encodes the recorded numerical bound so downstream\nconsumers can `[H3WedderburnReassembly]` and obtain the\nprecision-tagged identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.chiLambdaW0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.chiLambdaW0","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The character value χ_λ(w_0) = tr(ρ_λ(w_0)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.rhoLambdaW0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.rhoLambdaW0","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L125-L125","doc":"ρ_λ(w_0) for the longest element `w_0 ∈ S_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.rhoLambdaSigmaK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.rhoLambdaSigmaK","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L123-L123","doc":"ρ_λ(σ_k) for k = 1, …, n−1 (length `n − 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.dimLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.dimLambda","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Number of standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.SeminormalBlockData","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L106-L127","doc":"**Per-block Hoefsmit-seminormal representation data** for a\npartition `λ ⊢ n` of the Iwahori–Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`,\nparameterised over a generic commutative ring `R` (AGENTS.md §7c).\n\nThe fields encode the dimension `dim_λ` and the per-generator and\nlongest-word matrices in the Hoefsmit-seminormal basis indexed by\nstandard Young tableaux of shape `λ`.\n\nThe Python witness `option-e-phase1-gram-h6.witness.json` carries\nthe numerical instances at substrate `q_0 ∈ ℝ` for all 11 partitions\n`λ ⊢ 6`. A Mathlib-bridging follow-up will provide the symbolic\nconstruction at general `q` over a generic `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.dimLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.dimLambda","kind":"opaque","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L101-L104","doc":"The dimension of the irreducible representation `V_λ` of the\nsymmetric group `S_n` (and of `H_n(q)` over a commutative ring\n`R`), equal to the number of standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.positive","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.descending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.descending","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GramSeminormalBlock.Partition","kind":"structure","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GramSeminormalBlock.lean#L93-L99","doc":"A partition of `n` as a descending list of positive integers\nsumming to `n`. The empty list represents `n = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}